<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdullah ibn Saud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Abdullah bin Saud Al Saud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdullah ibn Saud was the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diriyah">Diriyah</a>, the first Saudi state, from 1814 to 1818. He faced the Ottoman-Egyptian invasion launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Muhammad Ali of Egypt</a> and led by Ibrahim Pasha, which overran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a> and besieged Diriyah. After surrendering in September 1818 he was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> and executed there in December the same year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdullah-ibn-saud.jpg" alt="Abdullah ibn Saud" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Félix Mengin ‏ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdullah_I_of_Saudi_Arabia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
